--------------------------------------------------------------------------
5/6. Assessment and proposal
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The matrix itself, the exact `mvn -pl regression-mcp-server -am clean
verify` command, and the no-automatic-smoke-test constraint are ALL already
correctly satisfied — confirmed by direct inspection, nothing to change
there.

One gap requires a change: `mvn validate` (full reactor, no `-pl` scoping)
is not run anywhere in CI. Proposing the following addition to the
`regression-mcp-server-security` job in `.github/workflows/main.yml` (added
as a new step immediately after "Set up JDK 21" and before "Verify the
local read-only MCP server", so a reactor-wide POM problem is caught before
spending time on the longer scoped build; running on both matrix legs since
the step is cheap — ~0.2s locally in Gate 16.0 — and matches how the other
three mandatory checks are already run per-OS in this job):

  - name: Validate the full reactor POMs
    run: mvn validate

Full corrected job block (steps only; job header/matrix unchanged) would
read:

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v5

      - name: Set up JDK 21
        uses: actions/setup-java@v5
        with:
          java-version: '21'
          distribution: 'temurin'

      - name: Validate the full reactor POMs
        run: mvn validate

      - name: Verify the local read-only MCP server
        run: mvn -pl regression-mcp-server -am clean verify

      - name: Require all MCP security tests to execute
        if: runner.os == 'Linux'
        run: |
          report_directory=regression-mcp-server/target/surefire-reports
          if [[ ! -d "$report_directory" ]]; then
            echo "MCP Surefire report directory is missing: $report_directory"
            exit 1
          fi

          shopt -s nullglob
          reports=("$report_directory"/TEST-*.xml)
          if (( ${#reports[@]} == 0 )); then
            echo "No MCP Surefire TEST-*.xml reports were produced."
            exit 1
          fi

          if grep -E 'skipped="[1-9][0-9]*"' "${reports[@]}"; then
            echo "MCP security tests must not be skipped on Linux."
            exit 1
          fi

This is a proposal only. No workflow file was edited in this gate.
